    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Ex7xgL6buSManKbGk6yqCQ)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent: touches only `sp-org-custom-highlight` (doc, `.el`, new test) and one README table cell.\n- No other open PR needs to merge before or after it.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `C-c h` (`sp-org-insert-inline-comment`) with an active region now wraps it in `@@comment:` ... `@@`.\n- Without a region it still inserts `@@comment:@@` with point inside.\n- Bug fixed: the mark stayed active over the new comment, so a second `C-c h` nested another comment inside it. The mark is now deactivated and point ends after the comment.\n- Multi-line regions: each non-blank line becomes its own comment.\n  - The font-lock rule matches one line only, so one comment across lines would export but never highlight.\n  - Indentation, trailing spaces and blank lines stay outside the markers.\n- A region containing `@@` is refused with a `user-error` (nothing changes).\n- A whitespace-only region counts as no region.\n- The edit is one undo step (`atomic-change-group`).\n- Point at the start or end of the region gives the same result.\n- Literate doc updated first, `.el` re-tangled (`tools/check-tangle.sh` shows only this module changed by this PR).\n- No `CHANGELOG.org` edit (nightly tidy owns it).\n\n## Tests\n\n- New `tests/sp-org-custom-highlight-test.el`, 9 ERT tests, all pass in Emacs 29.3 batch.\n- Run: `emacs -Q --batch -l tests/sp-org-custom-highlight-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit`\n\n## Manual testing checklist\n\n- [ ] In an Org buffer with no selection, `C-c h` inserts `@@comment:@@` with point inside.\n- [ ] Select a few words (point at the end), `C-c h`: they are wrapped and highlighted.\n- [ ] Same with point at the start of the selection (select backwards).\n- [ ] The selection disappears after wrapping; a second `C-c h` inserts an empty comment instead of nesting.\n- [ ] Select two lines and a blank line between, `C-c h`: each line gets its own comment, the blank line stays.\n- [ ] Select text containing `@@`: error message, buffer unchanged.\n- [ ] `C-z` (CUA undo) restores the original text in one step.\n- [ ] With the region made by mouse drag and by shift-arrows (CUA), both work.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiArdMeHBWipxrbLMU4)_",
